<article class="env-lemma" id="0BVX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BVX">Lemma <span data-tag="0BVX">49.7.2</span>.</a> Consider a cartesian diagram of schemes </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ Y' \ar[d]_{f'} \ar[r] &  Y \ar[d]^ f \\  X' \ar[r]^ g &  X }  \]
</div>
  <p> with $f$ locally of finite type. Let $R \subset Y$, resp. $R' \subset Y'$ be the closed subscheme cut out by the Kähler different of $f$, resp. $f'$. Then $Y' \to Y$ induces an isomorphism $R' \to R \times _ Y Y'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because $\Omega _{Y'/X'}$ is the pullback of $\Omega _{Y/X}$ (Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01V0" data-tag="01V0">29.33.10</a>) and then we can apply More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/07ZA" data-tag="07ZA">15.8.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>